Chris waters here with a gamespot news  update Blizzard has revealed the next  world of warcraft expansion lee jin wow  the expansion will add a new continent  called broken Isles it's never been  playable in World of Warcraft before but  was referenced in Warcraft freak what's  more Legion raises World of Warcraft's  level cap to 110 and introduces new  dungeons raids and artifact weapons but  the biggest announcement was the new  demon hunter hero class this melee  focused class can specializes either DPS  or tank but given the role of demon  hunters in Warcraft lore buzzard felt  that a healer spec wouldn't quite fit  demon hunters will be able to  metamorphosize into fell forms to be  able to hit harder and take more  punishment this is the first expansion  since 2014's warlords of Draenor world  of warcraft subscribers have been  slipping at a quick rate losing 1.5  million subscribers in the last three  months this expansion will likely help  boost those numbers at least for a short  amount of time a beta is expected later  this year meaning we can probably expect  the actual expansion to launch sometime  early in 2016 expect more details about  Legion at blizzcon this November and for  more news from gamescom stay tuned to  gamespot com splash news
 

